    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40763" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕductor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who leads</i> or <i>brings back</i> (very
			rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: plebis Romanae in urbem, *
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
				33 <i>fin.</i></span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterarum jam senescentium reductor ac
					reformator,</span>”
				i.e. <i>restorer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 8, 12, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
